.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.idea/

# Per-machine assistant permission grants. Machine-specific and rewritten on
# every session; nothing here is part of the project.
.claude/

# Package and model caches kept inside the project so they land on drive F
# and disappear with a single `rm -rf .cache`.
.cache/

# Langfuse bind-mount data. Recreated by `docker compose up`.
docker/

# Local-only working areas, by explicit decision (see CLAUDE.md): the test
# suite and the working notes, plans, reports and diagram sources.
tests/
docs/

# Vector index and BM25 corpus. Rebuilt by `python ingest.py`; a committed
# index would go stale against data/ with no signal that it had.
index/

# Runtime logs and crash-recovery checkpoints. Post-mortem artefacts, not
# project history.
logs/
*.log
runtime/

# Markdown: only README.md and the final report are tracked. Agent-facing
# docs (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, insights.md, handoff.md) are
# local-only by explicit decision -- they never leave this machine, so every
# session must run from this same checkout.
*.md
!README.md
!report/*.md

# evals/ is a declared exception to the local-only doc policy above (spec
# Sec13, decision D5): the golden dataset and its fixtures ship publicly,
# alongside the rest of the tracked project. Without this negation,
# evals/fixtures/poisoned_document.md is silently swallowed by the *.md
# rule above -- found live, while staging this stage's own commit.
!evals/fixtures/*.md

# The stage-10b failure taxonomy (spec Sec5.3/D9) is the same kind of
# public, tracked evaluation artefact -- the open-coding notes and the
# taxonomy they consolidate into ship alongside the golden dataset itself.
!evals/analysis/*.md
!evals/analysis/notes/*.md

# output/ holds generated reports. Ignore its contents, then re-include the
# reports and the placeholder: a stray file from a crashed run must not be
# picked up by a broad `git add`. Ignoring `output/` itself would make these
# negations unreachable.
output/*
!output/.gitkeep
!output/*.md

# Stage-10b sweep artefacts (span dumps, packs, checkpoints, results) --
# per-run-set, rebuilt by `python -m evals.run_eval`, never committed. The
# tracked outputs of a sweep are `evals/labels/human_labels.yaml` and
# `evals/analysis/` above, written by hand from reading a run, not the run
# directory itself.
runs/
